gstscream EOS panic fix
=======================

Without this patch, screamtx panics with "Screamtx callback srcpad.push
failed: Eos" when the upstream source emits its final buffer (e.g.
videotestsrc num-buffers=300 → EOS event). The push() returns the
benign FlowError::Eos which the original `.expect(..)` turns into a
SIGABRT, so the worker process dies before writing its result file.

This is a race window between screamtx's PadFlags::EOS check and the
actual srcpad.push() call. GStreamer 1.24's slightly different EOS
ordering (vs 1.16) makes the window reliably hit.

Apply with: patch -p1 < scream-eos-fix.patch  (run from project root)

--- a/scream/gstscream/src/screamtx/imp.rs
+++ b/scream/gstscream/src/screamtx/imp.rs
@@ -383,10 +383,31 @@
                         "gstscream Handling rtp buffer ssrc {ssrc}, seq {seq}, payload_type {payload_type}, timestamp {timestamp}, marker {marker} ");
                 }
                 drop(rtp_buffer);
-                (*stx)
-                    .srcpad
-                    .push(buffer)
-                    .expect("Screamtx callback srcpad.push failed");
+                // Downstream may have transitioned to EOS/Flushing between
+                // our PadFlags check above and this push (race window is
+                // unavoidable from a C callback). Treat those flow errors
+                // as benign and drop the buffer; only log on unexpected
+                // errors. The original `.expect(..)` panicked the worker
+                // process, which under GStreamer 1.24's slightly different
+                // EOS ordering became reliably reproducible.
+                match (*stx).srcpad.push(buffer) {
+                    Ok(_) => {}
+                    Err(gst::FlowError::Eos) | Err(gst::FlowError::Flushing) => {
+                        gst::info!(
+                            CAT,
+                            obj = (*stx).srcpad,
+                            "srcpad.push returned eos/flushing — dropping buffer"
+                        );
+                    }
+                    Err(err) => {
+                        gst::warning!(
+                            CAT,
+                            obj = (*stx).srcpad,
+                            "srcpad.push failed: {:?}",
+                            err
+                        );
+                    }
+                }
             }
         }
     } else {
